  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="13e5d43f-0171-4ebf-bf68-39abef4954ec"><problem><para>
      <para>Choose the expression that best describes the diagram.
          
          <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a4c39cadbd12167dc25e8a8977547823585c8403"/></media></figure></para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+5x+8\).</para><para>\((2x +5)(x +3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+14x + 23\).</para><para>\((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\).</para><para>\((2x +5)(x +3)\) is equivalent to \(30x^2\). </para></problem><solution><para>\((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\).</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
